<!-- noupdate="0" DELIBERATELY (W13) — see pb_home_hub/data/pb_sidebar.xml. -->
<odoo noupdate="0">

    <!-- OPERATE › Pay Run — ten rail items in one.

         Run Payroll · Pay Runs · Payslips · Results Grid · Import Data ·
         Pay & Deliver · Full & Final · Proration Audit · Retro Adjustments, plus
         the wizard-shaped Import flow that never had a rail entry at all. All of
         them survive as retired records pointing at live actions, so this item
         claims every one of their tags, the Pay Runs kanban's xmlid, and the
         three models the pay run is about.

         `hr.payslip.run` is claimed HERE and nowhere else now. It was the first
         of Cycle 1's two pinned double-claims — Approvals (OVERVIEW) and Pay
         Runs (PAY RUN) both claimed it, and the flat last-writer-wins index gave
         it to Pay Runs by ordering accident. It is a deliberate decision now,
         and it is the same one: a user opening a payslip run is in the pay run.

         `pb_import_wizard` is on the list although no rail item ever claimed it:
         the four-step import flow is a full-page client action reached from
         inside the Import cockpit, and before this cutover it left the rail with
         nothing selected.

         GATED SINCE ACCESS P4, in TWO LANES that are read as an OR.

         The lane written HERE is the older PERMISSION the payroll screens behind
         this entry already check: anybody who works a pay run holds
         `om_hr_payroll.group_hr_payroll_user`, directly or through the manager
         tier that implies it, so writing it down takes the door away from nobody
         who had a reason to be standing in it. The second lane — the ROLES that
         open this entry — is written onto the row by `pb_vendor_access`, which
         this module must never depend on. That is the whole reason this file
         names a permission and not a role.

         `(4, ref(…))` and never `(6, 0, …)`. This file is `noupdate="0"`, so an
         upgrade re-asserts what is written here, and a REPLACE would drop the
         demo persona's own group that `pb_demo` joins onto every gated entry
         (`pb_demo/models/demo_sidebar_access.py`). An ADD leaves it alone.
         Taking a permission back off this entry is therefore a migration, on
         purpose: the failure that matters is a gate that widens by accident,
         and this is the direction that cannot happen by itself.

         The shell still gates each lens from the ACL of the model behind it
         (W95). This decides only whether the door is on the wall. -->
    <record id="item_pay_run" model="pb.sidebar.item">
        <field name="section_id" ref="pb_sidebar.sec_payrun"/>
        <field name="groups_id"
               eval="[(4, ref('om_hr_payroll.group_hr_payroll_user'))]"/>
        <field name="name">Pay Run</field>
        <field name="icon">zap</field>
        <field name="sequence">10</field>
        <field name="action_xmlid">pb_payhub.action_pb_pay_hub</field>
        <field name="action_tag">pb_pay_hub</field>
        <field name="match_action_tags">pb_pay_hub,pb_payrun_wizard,pb_payslip_review,pb_payrun_results,pb_import,pb_import_wizard,pb_pay_delivery,pb_fullfinal,pb_proration,pb_retro</field>
        <field name="match_action_xmlids">pb_payruns.action_pb_payruns_kanban</field>
        <field name="match_models">hr.payslip.run,hr.payslip,hr.payroll.import.batch</field>
    </record>

</odoo>
